  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Z</mi></math> be the set of all integers,<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced open=\"{\" close=\"}\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo>:</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8722;</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mo>)</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#8804;</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced open=\"{\" close=\"}\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo>:</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#8804;</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced><mtext>&#160;and&#160;</mtext></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced open=\"{\" close=\"}\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo>:</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8722;</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mo>)</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>&#8722;</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mo>)</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#8804;</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced></math><br />If the total number of relations from <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mo>&#8745;</mo><mi>B</mi></math> to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mo>&#8745;</mo><mi>C</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>p</mi></msup></math>, then the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>p</mi></math> is:</p>"
  },
